rget-conditioned via a 1-D protein embedding* (e.g., a frozen sequence token embedding from a pretrained ProtBERT / ESM-2) concatenated to the decoder state, **plus** a single \\\"warhead\\\" substructure seed supplied as SMILES, \\u00e0 la M\\u00e9ndez-Lucio et al. 2020 / Lim et al. 2020. Falls back to unconditional SMILES generation if you want the simpler ARM.\\n- **Benchmark targets:** DRD2, JNK3, GSK3\\u03b2 as de facto standards. DRD2 vs DRD3 selectivity is an extra eval signal, not a separate arm unless you want it.\\n\\n### 2.2 Base generator \\u2014 to be confirmed\\nMy recommendation: **REINVENT-style SMILES-LM (RNN + attention), Priors & policies \\u00e0 la Olivecrona 2017 / Blaschke 2020**, augmented with the MCS-conditioned decoder head from Lim et al. 2020 for the target arm.\\n\\nWhy over graph generators (JT-VAE / GraphAF / DiffuMol):\\n- Mature toolchain for multi-property REINFORCE with a deterministic differentiable reward (likelihood-ratio, weighted-sum reward \\u2014 the \\\"augmented likelihood\\\" of REINVENT 3.0).\\n- Rejection sampling is trivial to bolt on.\\n- Graph generative models either (a) need score-matching on continuous features (DiffuMol) which is awkward for discrete QED/p-logP/affinity signals, or (b) need tree/fragment actions that complicate partial-credit REINFORCE.\\n\\nIf you'd rather pick a graph generator, say the word and I'll redesign the RL loop around STONED / MoFlow / GraphAF.\\n\\n### 2.3 Feedback-loop mechanism\\n**Recommended: rejection-sampling warm-up \\u2192 REINFORCE with weighted-sum reward (the REINVENT 3.0 \\\"augmented likelihood\\\").**\\n1. **Warm-up N1 batches** of rejection sampling from the prior, scoring each molecule with a weighted sum of property oracle calls; keep top-k to fine-tune the prior (SST \\u2014 \\\"sampling spoil-transfer\\\"). Cheaper, lower-variance than a pure-RL cold start.\\n2. **Policy gradient phase:** per-token REINFORCE with an \\\"augmented likelihood\\\" loss that adds a small scalar \\u03c3\\u00b7S(m) per molecule (S = reward, \\u03c3 like 60\\u2013120 in published settings). Experience replay / learning rate cliffs \\u00e0 la Blaschke 2020 to avoid catastrophic forgetting.\\n3. **Diversity-preservation term:** add to the reward an internal-diversity bonus *across the sampled batch* (mean pairwise 1\\u2212Tanimoto) and an explicit **alkane-chain penalty** (any molecule with >K contiguous sp3 carbons, K to be set in \\u00a74).\\n\\nRationale vs. the alternatives: pure rejection sampling throws away compute and saturates at the prior's modifiable set; pure REINFORCE on sparse 3-term reward has high variance; constrained decoding (e.g., constrained tree decode) can't enforce QED/affinity without an expensive search oracle per token.\\n\\n### 2.4 Datasets \\u2014 preview\\n- **Pre-training (language prior):** MOSES (\\u22481.6 M SMILES, already canonicalized) **or** a 1.5 M ChEMBL-28 random sample. MOSES gives us the public validity/uniqueness/novelty baseline numbers; ChEMBL aligns better with \\\"real-world drug-like\\\" distribution.\\n- **Distribution-learning eval:** MOSES test set + GuacaMol 10 K test (rediscovery / similarity /isomers /median molecules).\\n- **Target-conditioning fine-tuning:** ChEMBL28 DRD2 / JNK3 / GSK3\\u03b2 subsets (actives at standard cutoffs \\u2014 typically IC50/Ki \\u2264 1 \\u00b5M, see \\u00a74) + matched decoys (DUD-E if we can name them; otherwise ChEMBL-decoys from same target with Ki > 10 \\u00b5M). \\n- **Binding-affinity ground truth (held-out, not for RL training):** PDBbind-refined subset for evaluation of the affinity oracle only.\\n- *No code/datasets are touched in this design-only task \\u2014 these are dataset selections to be approved, not claims of having downloaded them.*\\n\\n### 2.5 Metrics \\u2014 three groups\\n\\n**(a) Chemical quality**\\n- Validity (canonical SMILES parses with RDKit).\\n- Uniqueness (unique among generated set; also reported @1 k / @10 k).\\n- Novelty (1 \\u2212 max Tanimoto to training set, threshold 0.4 for \\\"novel\\\" per MOSES convention).\\n- Internal validity violations: valency errors, kekulization failures, large-ring (\\u22658) sanity.\\n- Substructure realism: KL between BRICS-fragment histograms of generated vs training set; also PAINS / Brenk alert counts.\\n\\n**(b) Property scores (the feedback signals themselves, plus independent re-scoring)**\\n- **QED** (Bickerton 2012) via RDKit.\\n- **Penalized logP** = logP \\u2212 SA \\u2212 ringP, with SA from Ertl's SA score, ringP max(0, 6 \\u2212 rings)\\u00b7logP sigmoid-like; includes explicit long-alkane penalty in \\u00a72.3 (this is the \\\"avoid overlong chains\\\" criterion you mentioned).\\n- **Binding affinity surrogate** \\u2014 see \\u00a74.Q3 for choice. We will *re-score* the final generated set with a **different** held-out scorer (e.g., if RL used an ECFP-RF surrogate, re-score with a graph CNN or simple Vina on a stratified subsample) to detect surrogate overfitting.\\n\\n**(c) Structural diversity / hallucination indicators**\\n- Internal diversity = mean pairwise 1 \\u2212 Tani(Morgan r=2, 2048 b).\\n- Nearest-neighbour Tanimoto to training (mean, 10th percentile).\\n- \\\"Ultra-long carbon chain\\\" fraction: count of generated molecules with contiguous sp3-C chain length \\u2265 8 (threshold to confirm in \\u00a74).\\n- Scaffold entropy (Murcko scaffolds) and # unique scaffolds.\\n- Ring-size histogram (3-, 4-, \\u22658-membered fractions).\\n- Hallucination proxy: % generated molecules with >0 BRICS fragments not seen in training; % with novel Murcko scaffolds not seen in training (target: higher than baseline only if scaffolds are useful, capped).\\n\\n### 2.6 Arms \\u2014 controls and ablations\\n\\n| Arm | Feedback components |\\n|---|---|\\n| **A0** | base generator, no property feedback (prior only) |\\n| **A1** | + QED only |\\n| **A2** | + p-logP only (with SA + ringP + long-alkane penalty) |\\n| **A3** | + binding-affinity surrogate only |\\n| **A4** | + QED + p-logP + affinity (equal/tunable weights \\u2014 see \\u00a74.Q1) |\\n| **A5** | A4 + explicit diversity bonus in reward (tests whether diversity degrades under feedback) |\\n| **A6** | **Random-feedback control**: same generator, permuted molecule\\u2192score mapping inside each batch so drift over A0 comes from real signal, not gradient noise (cf. REINVENT 2.0 control) |\\n| **A7 (optional)** | A4 with a *different* affinity oracle (e.g., Vina/RF) than A3's \\u2014 oracle-bias sanity check |\\n\\nBudget per arm: 10 k generated molecules for evaluation + ~1 k\\u201310 k policy updates for training (range to finalize in \\u00a74.Q4).\\n\\n## 3. Required controls beyond ablations\\n- Fixed random seeds across arms (seed = {0,1,2} for reproducibility bands).\\n- Identical training set, identical evaluator, identical re-scoring protocol for every arm.\\n- Held-out PDBbind + held-out ChEMBL target panel for independent binding evaluation.\\n- A \\\"stash\\\" of pre-feedback generator samples kept so A5's diversity claims can be remeasured against the unconditioned distribution.\\n\\n## 4. Open questions (please confirm before approve_approach)\\n\\n1. Reward composition. Only QED, p-logP, affinity in the feedback (no SA, no ringP separately)? Equal weights or a specific scheme (e.g., 1\\u00b7QED + 0.5\\u00b7norm(p-logP) + 1\\u00b7tanh(affinity))? Is the long-alkane penalty additive inside p-logP or a separate term?\\n2. Target choice & bioactivity threshold. Just DRD2 / JNK3 / GSK3\\u03b2, or also DRD2-vs-DRD3 selectivity as a fourth signal? ChEMBL cutoff for \\\"active\\\" \\u2014 1 \\u00b5M IC50/Ki, 100 nM, or 10 nM? Per-target decoys from DUD-E or random ChEMBL?\\n3. Affinity oracle inside the RL loop. (i) Vina docking with cached pose \\u2014 slowest, most realistic; (ii) RF regressor on Morgan/ECFP trained on ChEMBL/PDBbind \\u2014 fast, risks surrogate overfitting; (iii) pretrained GNN affinity model (DimeNet / SchNet / AffinityNet) \\u2014 moderate cost. My default would be (ii) RF-ECFP trained per target, with A7 using (iii) for sanity check.\\n4. Generation budget per arm. Is 10 k molecules / arm acceptable, with ~5 k policy updates during the REINFORCE phase? Papers often use 100 k\\u20131 M \\u2014 please confirm scale so I can size audit/replay/log buffers correctly.\\n5. Score granularity. Per-molecule scalar at end of trajectory (REINVENT-vanilla) vs per-step token contribution (distributional RL)? I propose per-molecule \\u2014 lower variance, matches REINVENT 3.0 reports.\\n6. Conditioning. Target-conditioned (sequence embedding + MCS scaffold seed) or unconditional? \\\"Targeted molecule discovery\\\" suggests yes; please confirm whether scaffold conditioning is required or only target-sequence conditioning.\\n\\n## 5. Evidence I am leaning on (as known public benchmarks, not as our outcomes)\\n- MOSES public paper (Polykovskiy et al., 2020) \\u2014 validity/uniqueness/novelty reference protocol.\\n- GuacaMol benchmark (Brown et al., 2019) \\u2014 distribution-learning splits.\\n- REINVENT (Olivecrona et al. 2017) & REINVENT 2.0/3.0 (Blaschke et al. 2020) \\u2014 augmented-likelihood REINFORCE + SST.\\n- JT-VAE (Jin et al. 2018), GraphAF (Shi et al. 2020), MoFlow (Zang & Wang 2020), DiffuMol (Xu et al. 2022) \\u2014 graph-generator alternatives I considered.\\n- Conditional DGMs: Lim et al. 2020 (scaffold hopper), M\\u00e9ndez-Lucio et al. 2020 (ChemSpace).\\n- Penalized logP: Kusner et al. 2017 (GrammarVAE); SA score Ertl & Schuffenhauer 2009.\\n- DRD2/JNK3/GSK3\\u03b2 as De Novo Design benchmarks: Olivecrona 2017 / Blaschke 2020 / Brown 2019.\\n- DUD-E (Mysinger et al. 2012) for target-specific decoys.\\n\\nThese are cited as known reference points to anchor what \\\"good\\\" looks like, *not* as results we will report.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Ask:** Please answer \\u00a74's six questions (and confirm the generator + feedback-loop choices) before I move to `stage=result` with the full design document.\\n\", \"evidence\": \"Read /workspace/task.json (only file present). Confirmed the provided documents.track.md field contains a single line: \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\" No separate track.md file exists in /workspace. /workspace contains only task.json. No data, code, model weights, or configs shipped. researcher_topics is [] \\u2014 no pre-seeded clarifications. Environment per task.json: 24 vCPU, no GPU, system Python only, network disabled, no preinstalled deps. All other \\\"evidence\\\" cited in this plan is treated as background from public literature, not as project artefacts. Nothing in the repo was executed and no claims of having run any experiment are made.\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-4f122259-4d46-4252-adc1-34a79dc634fd", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 12}
